SUMMARY:The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:When a pious television "reporter" Melvin P. Thorpe (Dom DeLu
 ise) threatens to expose Miss Mona's (Dolly Parton) Texas brothel—the C
 hicken Ranch—to public scandal and close it down for good\, she vows no
 t to go down without a fight! With the help of her long-time secret sweet
 ie Sheriff Ed Earl Dodd (Burt Reynolds)\, the two join together to keep t
 he ranch open and\, naturally\, deepen their own romance along the way. S
 ing along through this extraordinary story about passion\, scandal\, comm
 unity\, and resistance! First premiering as a Broadway musical in 1978\, 
 The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas film adaptation was a critical mixed 
 bag upon its release\, but the people loved it! The film brought in the b
 iggest weekend box-office opening for a musical up to that point in time 
 and was nominated for two Golden Globes: Best Motion Picture - Musical or
  Comedy and Best Actress in a Motion Picture or Comedy for Parton. Musica
 l numbers include two of Parton's biggest hits: "Hard Candy Christmas" an
 d "I Will Always Love You." [114 min\; comedy\, musical\, romance\; Engli
 sh]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  When a pious television "reporter" Melv
 in P. Thorpe (Dom DeLuise) threatens to expose Miss Mona's (Dolly Parton)
  Texas brothel—the Chicken Ranch—to public scandal and close it down 
 for good\, she vows not to go down without a fight! With the help of her 
 long-time secret sweetie Sheriff Ed Earl Dodd (Burt Reynolds)\, the two j
 oin together to keep the ranch open and\, naturally\, deepen their own ro
 mance along the way. Sing along through this extraordinary story about pa
 ssion\, scandal\, community\, and resistance! First premiering as a Broad
 way musical in 1978\, <i>The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas</i> film ada
 ptation was a critical mixed bag upon its release\, but the people loved 
 it! The film brought in the biggest weekend box-office opening for a musi
 cal up to that point in time and was nominated for two Golden Globes: Bes
 t Motion Picture - Musical or Comedy and Best Actress in a Motion Picture
  or Comedy for Parton. Musical numbers include two of Parton's biggest hi
 ts: "Hard Candy Christmas" and "I Will Always Love You." [114 min\; comed
 y\, musical\, romance\; English]</p>
